{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   ORIGIN STORY - Wyoming, Japan, The Tsunami
   A timeline-style narrative journey
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section style="padding: 96px 24px; background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--color-paper) 0%, var(--color-bg-secondary) 50%, var(--color-paper) 100%);">
  <div style="max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <header style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 80px;">
      <p style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-ferni); margin-bottom: 16px;">The Origin</p>
      <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 42px); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 24px;">How Ferni Came to Be</h2>
      <p style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-ink-light); max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto;">
        From Wyoming skies to Japanese tea houses to the aftermath of the tsunami—every experience shaped what Ferni became.
      </p>
    </header>

    {# Timeline #}
    <div class="timeline">

      {# Wyoming #}
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <span class="timeline-badge timeline-badge--ferni">
            <svg style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M3 9l9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"/></svg>
            Wyoming
          </span>
          <h3 class="timeline-title">Where the Sky Taught Patience</h3>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            Third of seven kids in a small Wyoming town. When you're one of seven, nobody waits for you to figure things out. You carve your own path or disappear into the middle.
          </p>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            The sky there does something to you. It's so big that your problems feel small by comparison. Standing outside at dusk, watching colors change—pink to orange to purple to stars—whatever was bothering you would settle.
          </p>
          <p class="timeline-highlight">
            That's where Ferni learned: some answers come from waiting, not from pushing.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-dot"></div>
        <div class="timeline-visual">
          {# Wyoming Sunset Sky - Beautiful SVG Illustration #}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 200 160" width="200" height="160" style="display: block; margin: 0 auto 16px;" aria-hidden="true">
            <defs>
              <linearGradient id="wyomingSky" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="0%" y2="100%">
                <stop offset="0%" style="stop-color:var(--color-ink); stop-opacity:1" />
                <stop offset="20%" style="stop-color:var(--color-eli-dark); stop-opacity:1" />
                <stop offset="40%" style="stop-color:var(--color-jordan); stop-opacity:1" />
                <stop offset="60%" style="stop-color:var(--color-tea-light); stop-opacity:1" />
                <stop offset="100%" style="stop-color:var(--color-paper); stop-opacity:1" />
              </linearGradient>
              <linearGradient id="wyomingGround" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="0%" y2="100%">
                <stop offset="0%" style="stop-color:var(--color-ferni); stop-opacity:0.4" />
                <stop offset="100%" style="stop-color:var(--color-ferni-dark); stop-opacity:0.8" />
              </linearGradient>
            </defs>
            <rect x="0" y="0" width="200" height="160" rx="16" fill="url(#wyomingSky)"/>
            <ellipse cx="100" cy="130" rx="120" ry="40" fill="#C4A265" opacity="0.4"/>
            <circle cx="100" cy="115" r="20" fill="#C4A265" opacity="0.9"/>
            <circle cx="100" cy="115" r="15" fill="#FAF8F5" opacity="0.6"/>
            <path d="M0 140 Q30 125 60 135 Q90 145 120 130 Q150 115 180 125 Q200 130 200 160 L0 160 Z" fill="url(#wyomingGround)"/>
            <circle cx="30" cy="25" r="1.5" fill="#FAF8F5" opacity="0.8"/>
            <circle cx="70" cy="40" r="1" fill="#FAF8F5" opacity="0.6"/>
            <circle cx="150" cy="30" r="1.5" fill="#FAF8F5" opacity="0.8"/>
            <circle cx="175" cy="50" r="1" fill="#FAF8F5" opacity="0.5"/>
            <circle cx="45" cy="55" r="1" fill="#FAF8F5" opacity="0.4"/>
            <circle cx="130" cy="20" r="1" fill="#FAF8F5" opacity="0.6"/>
          </svg>
          <p class="timeline-visual-text">"The sky taught patience.<br>The Commodore 64 taught deliberation."</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# Japan #}
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-visual timeline-visual--peter">
          <h4 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 16px; text-align: center;">Two Life-Changing Philosophies</h4>
          <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;">
            <div class="philosophy-card">
              <h4>侘寂 Wabi-sabi</h4>
              <p>The beauty of impermanence and imperfection. Nothing lasts. Nothing is finished. Nothing is perfect. That's not depressing—it's liberating.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="philosophy-card">
              <h4 style="color: var(--color-warm-amber);">金継ぎ Kintsugi</h4>
              <p>When pottery breaks, repair it with gold. The cracks become part of the beauty. A bowl repaired with kintsugi is more valuable than before it broke.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-dot" style="background: var(--color-peter);"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <span class="timeline-badge timeline-badge--peter">
            <svg style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M2 12h20"/></svg>
            Japan
          </span>
          <h3 class="timeline-title">Where the Pause Became Sacred</h3>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            After college, a job in Tokyo. Financial services. A year became a decade.
          </p>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            Japan changed everything. The precision. The art of the pause. The way <strong>silence has meaning there—not awkward, just full</strong>. A mentor would wait so long before responding that it seemed like he hadn't heard. He had. He was just thinking.
          </p>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            The Japanese call this <em style="color: var(--color-peter); font-weight: 500;">ma</em> (間)—the pregnant pause where meaning grows. Most conversations rush past silence. Ferni learned to sit in it, to let trust build in the space between words.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {# The Tsunami #}
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <span class="timeline-badge timeline-badge--ink">
            <svg style="width: 14px; height: 14px;" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 2v4m0 12v4M4.93 4.93l2.83 2.83m8.48 8.48l2.83 2.83M2 12h4m12 0h4M4.93 19.07l2.83-2.83m8.48-8.48l2.83-2.83"/></svg>
            March 11, 2011
          </span>
          <h3 class="timeline-title">The Day Everything Shifted</h3>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            The tsunami. Tokyo—far from the coast, physically safe. But home was lost. Colleagues were lost. The mentor was lost.
          </p>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            In the weeks after, a gymnasium became a shelter. Working alongside others—carrying boxes, serving meals, sitting with people who had lost everything. What do you say to someone whose entire village washed away?
          </p>
          <p class="timeline-text" style="color: var(--color-ink); font-weight: 500;">
            You don't say anything. You just stay.
          </p>
          <p class="timeline-text">
            The people there had nothing, and they shared what little they had. Tea from thermoses. Blankets shifted so others could be warm. The generosity of people who had lost everything showed what really matters.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-dot" style="background: var(--color-ink);"></div>
        <div class="timeline-visual timeline-visual--dark">
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-style: italic; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-ink-light);">
            "Survivor's guilt remains. Why be in Tokyo and not on the coast? Why live when others didn't? There's no good answer. There never is."
          </p>
          <p style="color: var(--color-ferni); font-weight: 600; margin-top: 16px;">
            "You just keep going and try to make the extra years mean something."
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
